diff --git a/changes/2073.bugfix.rst b/changes/2073.bugfix.rst
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..52d7bee
--- /dev/null
+++ b/changes/2073.bugfix.rst
@@ -0,0 +1 @@
+Flatpak apps no longer request access to the DBus session bus by default, as this breaks the Flatpak sandbox. Apps that need session bus access can request it by adding ``finish_arg."socket=session-bus" = true`` to their app configuration.
diff --git a/docs/reference/platforms/linux/flatpak.rst b/docs/reference/platforms/linux/flatpak.rst
index eab3c9f..0cf28b3 100644
--- a/docs/reference/platforms/linux/flatpak.rst
+++ b/docs/reference/platforms/linux/flatpak.rst
@@ -96,13 +96,18 @@ Briefcase adds the following finish arguments by default:
 * ``filesystem=xdg-config``
 * ``filesystem=xdg-data``
 * ``filesystem=xdg-documents``
-* ``socket=session-bus``
 
 These can be disabled by explicitly setting their value to ``False``; for example, to
 disable audio access, you would specify::
 
     finish_arg."socket=pulseaudio" = false
 
+Briefcase does not grant access to the DBus session bus by default, as this breaks the
+Flatpak sandbox. If your app needs access to the session bus, you can add it as a finish
+argument::
+
+    finish_arg."socket=session-bus" = true
+
 ``flatpak_runtime_repo_alias``
 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
 
